{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the teacher</b> — Yefet says: that 'the teacher' is the prophet, for he teaches them the way of righteousness; therefore the good comes to them. And he mentioned 'teacher' [מורה] and 'latter rain' [מלקוש] like: 'with the jawbone of an ass, ass-heap, thirty towns' [and] 'thirty towns' — 'who kindles the kindling, that a man may kindle.' But in my opinion: it is like יורה [the early rain], and he said את המורה לצדקה ['a teacher for righteousness'] like: 'sun of righteousness and healing in its wings.'" "<b>And the meaning of 'at the first'</b> — in the first month. For always there are many days between the season of the יורה [early rain], which is like the מורה [teacher], and the season of the מלקוש [latter rain]; but in the first month both come — and this is a matter of miracle, as it is also: 'for YHWH has done a great thing.'"], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The two examples of wordplay (שמש/חמור and יבער/המבעיר) are rendered hyper-literally; the logic of Ibn Ezra's grammatical parallel is compressed and opaque in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:47.474757706Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}